WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.746
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:15.913
Unit twenty-four: Buddhist Philosophy. Today you will describe a tradition using relative clauses with 'in which'.

4
00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:18.877
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:22.776
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.525
Buddhism.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:28.851
Buddhism means the tradition founded on the teachings of the Buddha.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.168
Buddhism shapes festivals, ethics and daily habits in Cambodia.

9
00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.238
Your turn. Say: Buddhism.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.008
Buddhism.

11
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.972
Impermanence.

12
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:46.608
Impermanence means the teaching that all things are constantly changing.

13
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:50.586
Impermanence reminds us that no condition lasts forever.

14
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.905
Your turn. Say: Impermanence.

15
00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.058
Impermanence.

16
00:00:58.817 --> 00:00:59.771
Suffering.

17
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:05.093
Suffering means the dissatisfaction and pain inherent in unexamined life.

18
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:08.763
The first noble truth acknowledges suffering honestly.

19
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.654
Your turn. Say: Suffering.

20
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.513
Suffering.

21
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.321
Mindfulness.

22
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:22.812
Mindfulness means paying deliberate, non-judgmental attention to the present moment.

23
00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:26.577
Mindfulness trains attention through breath and posture.

24
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:30.161
Your turn. Say: Mindfulness.

25
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.291
Mindfulness.

26
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.237
Compassion.

27
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:41.200
Compassion means sympathy joined with the wish to relieve another's suffering.

28
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:45.291
Compassion is central to Mahayana and Theravada practice.

29
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:48.234
Your turn. Say: Compassion.

30
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.113
Compassion.

31
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.874
Middle Way.

32
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:58.450
Middle Way means the path between indulgence and harsh self-denial.

33
00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.269
The Buddha taught the Middle Way after trying extreme asceticism.

34
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:05.454
Your turn. Say: Middle Way.

35
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.348
Middle Way.

36
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.142
Non-self.

37
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.636
Non-self means the teaching that there is no fixed, permanent self.

38
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.759
Non-self challenges the idea of a lasting inner essence.

39
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.142
Your turn. Say: Non-self.

40
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.048
Non-self.

41
00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:28.703
Ethics.

42
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:33.017
Ethics means principles governing right and wrong conduct.

43
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:36.580
Buddhist ethics begins with the intention not to harm.

44
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:40.045
Your turn. Say: Ethics.

45
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:43.913
Ethics.

46
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.328
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:49.183 --> 00:02:54.785
Visal, my grandmother says Buddhism is not a religion but a way of living. What does she mean?

48
00:02:55.883 --> 00:03:02.318
She describes a tradition in which compassion is central and practice matters more than doctrine.

49
00:03:03.417 --> 00:03:05.532
Practice like going to the pagoda?

50
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:15.713
That, and mindfulness. It is a discipline in which attention is trained to notice impermanence rather than cling to it.

51
00:03:16.817 --> 00:03:18.944
And how does that help in daily life?

52
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:29.831
It offers a path along which one can face suffering with equanimity. This is a view of life in which kindness is the measure of wisdom.

53
00:03:30.967 --> 00:03:32.908
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.818
Grammar focus: Relative clauses with in which.

55
00:03:37.118 --> 00:03:38.397
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:42.023
It is a tradition in which compassion is central.

57
00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:46.321
Mindfulness is a discipline in which attention is trained.

58
00:03:47.217 --> 00:03:50.586
It is a view of life in which kindness is the measure of wisdom.

59
00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:59.747
Preposition + which/whom = formal relative clause: a tradition in which, the path along which, the person to whom. Never 'in that' or 'in what'.

60
00:04:00.483 --> 00:04:05.284
Be careful! Don't say: It is a tradition in that compassion is central.

61
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:10.371
Say: It is a tradition in which compassion is central.

62
00:04:10.671 --> 00:04:12.786
Preposition + which (not 'that').

63
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.392
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.259
The Middle Way.

65
00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:27.118
Buddhism arose in India some 2,500 years ago and spread across Asia, taking root in Cambodia as a living part of national culture.

66
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:35.682
At its core are four noble truths, which acknowledge suffering, trace it to craving, and describe a path along which it can be overcome.

67
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:44.158
The Buddha rejected both indulgence and extreme asceticism, advocating a Middle Way in which balance, not denial, guides conduct.

68
00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:52.693
Central teachings, such as impermanence and non-self, challenge the assumption that we possess a fixed identity to which we must cling.

69
00:04:53.700 --> 00:05:00.227
Ethics and compassion follow naturally, since a person who understands interdependence has little reason to harm others.

70
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:05.358
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:06.217 --> 00:05:08.808
It is a tradition blank compassion is central.

72
00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.622
A, in which. B, in that. C, which in.

73
00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.062
The answer is A: in which.

74
00:05:19.217 --> 00:05:21.715
The teaching that all things change is blank.

75
00:05:22.015 --> 00:05:26.145
A, impermanence. B, non-self. C, mindfulness.

76
00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.141
The answer is A: impermanence.

77
00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:36.630
The path between indulgence and self-denial is the blank.

78
00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:40.722
A, Middle Way. B, first truth. C, ethics.

79
00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.522
The answer is A: Middle Way.

80
00:05:47.683 --> 00:05:49.369
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:49.669 --> 00:05:58.083
A, It is a practice in which attention is trained.. B, It is a practice in that attention is trained.. C, It is a practice which in attention trained..

82
00:06:01.633 --> 00:06:05.525
The answer is A: It is a practice in which attention is trained..

83
00:06:06.683 --> 00:06:09.194
According to the reading, the Buddha rejected…

84
00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:14.912
A, balance. B, indulgence and extreme asceticism. C, ethics.

85
00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:21.836
The answer is B: indulgence and extreme asceticism.

86
00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:26.371
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:27.217 --> 00:06:30.726
How do Buddhist ideas influence daily life in Cambodia?

88
00:06:47.517 --> 00:06:49.168
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:49.468 --> 00:07:22.195
Buddhist ideas influence daily life in Cambodia through festivals, family customs and the way people think about merit and kindness. Many people give food to monks each morning, and the pagoda serves as a place in which communities gather and children learn. Teachings on impermanence and compassion encourage patience during hardship and generosity toward others. These ideas shape ethics as much as ritual.

90
00:07:22.495 --> 00:07:24.356
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:29.725
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clauses with in which.

92
00:07:30.025 --> 00:07:34.152
Today's value is compassion. Care about the suffering of others and help.

93
00:07:34.452 --> 00:07:37.244
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:07:37.544 --> 00:07:41.624
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

